-- title:
--   Rational integral function separating two supersingular places, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q = 3$ and a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $q$, in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$, and write $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ for its residue field. Let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$ (the subfield of $(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)((t))$ generated by the reductions of $j$ and of $j(M'\cdot)$) over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, whose members are exactly the places belonging to $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\,q\,M'\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)$, i.e. those satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace`. Assume the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$ of intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, where $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ is the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full level-$M'$ function field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M' = \mathbb Q(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\,M')$. Let $R_0$ be a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ on $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ with values in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\,(\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A)\,M'$: a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ together with a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto that field whose kernel is the maximal ideal, extending the residue map of $A$, together with a map on places preserving degrees and orders. Assume $hR_0$: for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, that image is $R_0$-integral and its $R_0$-residue is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$ modulo the maximal ideal of $A$. Finally let $s \ne s'$ be two elements of $W$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\,M'$ whose image under the coefficientwise embedding into $\overline{\mathbb Q}((t))$, viewed in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$, lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and satisfies: at every place $P$ of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, if $\mathrm{ord}_P$ of the image of $jq$ is $\ge 0$ then $\mathrm{ord}_P(g) \ge 0$; the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subrings of both $s$ and $s'$; and the values $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ and $s'.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that residue, elements of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$, are distinct.
--
--   This is the separation statement used on the supersingular covering of the full-level modular curve: two distinct supersingular places of the reduction are distinguished by the value of a single rational level-$M'$ modular function which is $R_0$-integral and regular wherever $j$ is. It is invoked in the constructions of node charts, of descent data for Drinfeld-type rings and of invariant elements avoiding prescribed valuation subrings at the auxiliary level, in the $q = 3$ branch of that analysis.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_exists_rational_integral_evalAt_ne_of_ne_ssPlaces_of_eq_three.lean

